message.content:
Below is a minimal, self‑contained example of a “flip‑card” that rotates (in 3D) when you hover over it.  
Copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser – you’ll see a card that flips around its Y‑axis when the mouse hovers over it.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Set up the container with perspective so the 3D effect looks good */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D transform */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* 2️⃣  The card itself – we’ll rotate this */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;  /* Needed for 3D children */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth animation */
}

/* 3️⃣  Flip the card on hover */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* Rotate 180° around the Y‑axis */
}

/* 4️⃣  Front & back faces – positioned absolutely */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden; /* Hide the back side when facing away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
}

/* 5️⃣  Front face styling */
.card-front {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b);
}

/* 6️⃣  Back face styling – rotated 180° so it shows after flip */
.card-back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6a11cb, #2575fc);
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* Flip it so it appears correctly */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | `perspective` on the wrapper | Gives depth to the 3D transform. |
| 2 | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on the card | Allows child elements to maintain 3D positioning. |
| 3 | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| 4 | `backface-visibility: hidden` on faces | Hides the backside of each face when it’s not facing the viewer. |
| 5–6 | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on the back face | Positions the back face so it becomes visible after the card flips. |

Feel free to tweak the colors, size, or rotation axis (`rotateX`, `rotateZ`) to fit your design. Happy coding!
